choc-webview2-permissions.patch: the WebView2 backend asks the app before it
grants a page a permission, clipboard reads included (B446, ADR-196).

Base:     choc a08bfd84494921700703a8433b9d1a304edfafd2 (the libs/choc pin)
Applied:  at configure time, to a build-tree copy of libs/choc/choc, by
          libs/patches/apply_patch.cmake, after choc-webview2-navigation.patch.
          The submodule is never edited.
Checked:  tools/choc_patch_check.py (./verify fast).

PURPOSE. choc's WebView2 PermissionRequested handler grants every clipboard
read a page asks for, and an app cannot change that: the handler and the
ICoreWebView2 object are private. This adds one option,
WebView::Options::allowPermission (kind), which the handler consults when it
is set: true grants the permission, false refuses it. horde's Windows backend
(src/gui/hypersaw_gui_win.cpp) refuses every kind, so page script cannot read
the clipboard; PASTE reads it natively instead (hzPasteState), as on macOS.

DEFAULT UNCHANGED. The patch only adds lines. With the option left empty the
handler runs exactly as upstream: clipboard reads are granted and every other
kind is left to WebView2.

SEPARATE FILE. It is carried apart from the navigation patch so that either
can be dropped when upstream takes its half. Each is made against the pristine
pin and changes no line the other's hunks rely on, so each applies alone as
well as in order; tools/choc_patch_check.py checks both.

UPSTREAM STATUS. Not yet proposed. A follow-up comment on the navigation-option
request (Tracktion/choc#111) is drafted for the human's review; posting it
outside the fleet takes the human's explicit yes.

REMOVAL CONDITION. Delete this patch and its wiring (libs/patches/README.md
lists every piece) when the pinned choc provides an equivalent permission
hook. If the upstream shape differs, port src/gui/hypersaw_gui_win.cpp to it
in the same change. Any bump of libs/choc turns tools/choc_patch_check.py red
until the Base line above is updated, so the question is asked at every bump.

--- a/choc/gui/choc_WebView.h
+++ b/choc/gui/choc_WebView.h
@@ -132,6 +132,26 @@
         /// by default, so you can avoid a flash of white while it's loading the
         /// content.
         bool transparentBackground = false;
+
+        /// The kinds of permission that allowPermission is asked about.
+        enum class PermissionKind
+        {
+            clipboardRead,
+            microphone,
+            camera,
+            geolocation,
+            notifications,
+            otherSensors,
+            other         ///< any kind not listed above
+        };
+
+        /// Optional. If set, this is called on the message thread each time the
+        /// page requests a permission. The permission is granted if it returns
+        /// true and refused if it returns false, with no prompt either way. Leave
+        /// it empty for the default behaviour, which grants clipboard reads and
+        /// leaves every other kind to the browser's own handling. Currently
+        /// implemented by the WebView2 (Windows) backend.
+        std::function<bool(PermissionKind)> allowPermission;
 
         /// On OSX there's some custom code to intercept copy/paste keys, which
         /// otherwise wouldn't work by default. This lets you turn that off if you
@@ -1736,10 +1756,35 @@
             COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND permissionKind;
             args->get_PermissionKind (std::addressof (permissionKind));
 
+            if (ownerPimpl.options.allowPermission)
+            {
+                auto allowed = ! deletionCheckerRef->deleted
+                                && ownerPimpl.options.allowPermission (getPermissionKind (permissionKind));
+
+                args->put_State (allowed ? COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_STATE_ALLOW
+                                         : COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_STATE_DENY);
+                return S_OK;
+            }
+
             if (permissionKind == COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_CLIPBOARD_READ)
                 args->put_State (COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_STATE_ALLOW);
 
             return S_OK;
+        }
+
+        static Options::PermissionKind getPermissionKind (COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND kind)
+        {
+            switch (kind)
+            {
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_CLIPBOARD_READ:   return Options::PermissionKind::clipboardRead;
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_MICROPHONE:       return Options::PermissionKind::microphone;
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_CAMERA:           return Options::PermissionKind::camera;
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_GEOLOCATION:      return Options::PermissionKind::geolocation;
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_NOTIFICATIONS:    return Options::PermissionKind::notifications;
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_OTHER_SENSORS:    return Options::PermissionKind::otherSensors;
+                case COREWEBVIEW2_PERMISSION_KIND_UNKNOWN_PERMISSION:
+                default:                                            return Options::PermissionKind::other;
+            }
         }
 
         HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE Invoke (ICoreWebView2*, ICoreWebView2WebResourceRequestedEventArgs* args) override
